  <section class="mp-section" id="campaign-types"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">01 / Start with the account relationship</p><h2>Choose the phone work<br>that moves your pipeline.</h2><p>A new prospect and someone who asked for information need different preparation. Build separate account groups and talk tracks.</p></div><div class="mp-scope-grid">
    <article><span class="mp-step">New business outreach</span><h3>Open a relevant conversation.</h3><p>Introduce your offer to suitable businesses, identify the responsible buyer and establish whether a discussion is worthwhile.</p><p class="mp-output"><strong>Go deeper</strong><a href="/services/b2b-cold-calling/">See the cold calling process</a> for call preparation, sample dialogue and response handling.</p></article>
    <article><span class="mp-step">Lead and event follow-up</span><h3>Act on existing interest.</h3><p>Work the agreed enquiry or event list with the original context. Confirm the current need and route the contact to a meeting, further follow-up or closure.</p><p class="mp-output"><strong>Focused event support</strong><a href="/services/trade-show-lead-follow-up/">Trade show lead follow-up</a> covers the post-event campaign.</p></article>
    <article><span class="mp-step">Dormant accounts</span><h3>Check what has changed.</h3><p>Revisit suitable older conversations with a specific reason. Learn whether timing, priorities or provider arrangements make the account worth reopening.</p><p class="mp-output"><strong>Focused recovery support</strong><a href="/services/lead-reactivation/">Lead reactivation services</a> explain work with inactive records.</p></article>
  </div><p class="mp-caption">Scope one group or coordinate several. Each needs a defined source, contact status, exclusions and next action.</p></div></section>

  <section class="mp-section mp-paper" id="programme-scope"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">02 / Know what you are buying</p><h2>A programme with<br>named responsibilities.</h2><p class="mp-section-lead">A telemarketing agency should explain what it will deliver before the first call and what happens when a buyer responds.</p><ul class="mp-checks"><li><strong>Campaign preparation:</strong> account groups, approved claims, talk tracks, qualification and contact rules.</li><li><strong>Human execution:</strong> live calls, requested callbacks, referrals and agreed follow-up.</li><li><strong>Sales routing:</strong> relevant appointments, further nurture, unsuitable accounts and stop requests.</li><li><strong>Campaign review:</strong> activity, buyer responses, meeting outcomes and recommended adjustments.</li></ul><p>You supply product knowledge, commercial decisions, approved proof and access to sellers. We agree data preparation, systems, reporting and the work CallTeam manages in the proposal.</p><p>For a wider managed prospecting function, explore <a href="/services/outsourced-sdr/">outsourced SDR services</a>. For the whole account-to-meeting engagement, see <a href="/services/b2b-lead-generation/">B2B lead generation services</a>.</p></div>
    <aside class="mp-note"><p class="mp-label">Illustrative handoff / service enquiry</p><h3>Give sales the reason<br>behind the booking.</h3><dl><div><dt>Account</dt><dd>Within the agreed industry, size and territory.</dd></div><div><dt>Contact</dt><dd>Operations lead evaluating a recurring service problem.</dd></div><div><dt>Interest</dt><dd>Wants to understand coverage before the next contract review.</dd></div><div><dt>Unknown</dt><dd>Budget and final purchasing authority need discovery.</dd></div><div><dt>Next owner</dt><dd>Your seller, with the agreed meeting purpose and date.</dd></div></dl><p class="mp-small">Fictional example fields. A booking and a sales opportunity are separate stages.</p></aside>
  </div><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-tool-band"><div><h3>Turn your offer into a campaign brief.</h3><p>Explore target buyers, a conversation approach and useful resources before deciding the scope.</p></div><a class="mp-button" href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/">See How We’d Run Your Campaign ↗</a></div></div></section>

  <section class="mp-section" id="contact-controls"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">03 / Put contact controls in the brief</p><h2>Define how the campaign<br>represents your business.</h2><p>Confirm the destination, number type, calling method, approved identity, local calling windows and suppression workflow before activation.</p></div>
    <div class="mp-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Canada and US telemarketing planning; scroll horizontally on smaller screens"><table class="mp-market-table"><caption class="sr-only">Selected Canada and United States telemarketing considerations</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Market</th><th scope="col">Rule to understand</th><th scope="col">Put into the campaign brief</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Canada</th><td>Business calls are exempt from the National DNCL rules. Registration, internal do-not-call lists and the applicable Telemarketing Rules still apply.</td><td>Confirm client and provider registrations, account classification, caller identification, local calling windows and how stop requests are recorded.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">United States</th><td>The FTC extended prohibitions against misrepresentations to B2B telemarketing in 2024. A business audience does not settle every federal or state calling requirement.</td><td>Review the actual numbers, technology and territories. Agree approved claims, opt-out handling and the rules applicable to the planned campaign.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Follow-up channels</th><td>Permission to make a call does not automatically establish permission for an email, text or automated message.</td><td>Confirm each proposed channel separately, including its consent, identification and opt-out requirements.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Planning a Canadian territory or a Canada-to-US assignment? See <a href="/b2b-lead-generation-canada/">our Canadian lead generation service</a> for coverage, language and scheduling.</p>
    <p>Keep a stop request attached to the account across the dialler, CRM and later follow-up lists. Name the person who updates those records and the person who checks that the change has reached every campaign system.</p><p>These are selected planning points, not a complete legal assessment. Our <a href="/articles/b2b-cold-calling-compliance-global/">global B2B calling compliance guide</a> covers the broader review framework.</p>
    <p class="mp-source-note">Official sources reviewed 29 October 2026:</p><ul class="mp-source-list"><li><a href="https://crtc.gc.ca/eng/phone/telemarketing/biz.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CRTC: business-to-business calls and client responsibilities</a>; <a href="https://crtc.gc.ca/eng/phone/telemarketing/reg.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">registration and exempt telemarketers</a>.</li><li><a href="https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases/2024/03/ftc-implements-new-protections-businesses-against-telemarketing-fraud-affirms-protections-against-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FTC: B2B telemarketing fraud protections</a>; <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-CC-PURL-gpo252648/pdf/GOVPUB-CC-PURL-gpo252648.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FCC consumer guide: calling technology and number types</a>.</li></ul>
  </div></section>

